{
  "id": "l01",
  "number": 1,
  "chapter": 1,
  "title": "The Nominative Case",
  "subtitle": "Masculine nouns ending in -a · Present tense third person verbs",
  "tags": [
    "Cases",
    "Masc. -a nouns",
    "Present tense"
  ],
  "minutes": 15,
  "revision": null,
  "teach": [
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "title": "Nouns in -a",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "eyebrow": "Grammar — Part A",
          "html": "Nouns in <em>-a</em>"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "html": "The <strong>Nominative Case</strong> is used to indicate the subject of a sentence. In Pāli, words change their endings to show their grammatical role. For masculine nouns ending in <em>-a</em>, the base drops the <em>-a</em> and adds an ending."
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "For masculine nouns ending in -a:",
          "formulas": [
            "Singular: base + <em>-o</em> <span>|</span> The man = nar<em>o</em>",
            "Plural:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;base + <em>-ā</em> <span>|</span> Men / The men = nar<em>ā</em>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Base: <em>nara</em> (man)",
          "head": [
            "Case",
            "Singular",
            "Plural"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Nominative",
              "nar<span class=\"decl-ending\">o</span>",
              "nar<span class=\"decl-ending\">ā</span>"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 2,
          "eyebrow": "Grammar — Part B",
          "html": "Verbs — Present Tense"
        },
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "html": "Like nouns, verbs change ending depending on who is performing the action (I, you, he/they). For now we will focus on the third person (he/she/it/they)."
        },
        {
          "type": "rule",
          "title": "For third person present tense verbs:",
          "formulas": [
            "Singular: root + <em>-ti</em> <span>|</span> He goes = gaccha<em>ti</em>",
            "Plural:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;root + <em>-nti</em> <span>|</span> They go = gaccha<em>nti</em>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Base: <em>gaccha</em> (go, from √gam)",
          "head": [
            "Person",
            "Singular",
            "Plural"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Third",
              "gaccha<span class=\"decl-ending\">ti</span>",
              "gaccha<span class=\"decl-ending\">nti</span>"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
